III. It has grown dark, the waters weep, the mantle of night covers us;
It is the time of the stars' shimmering, the sprinkling of dew upon the grass,
Of the dead souls' emergence from the grave, the time of their quiet song.

Translated Content 29:
III. Darkness has fallen, the waters weep, the mantle of night covers us;
It is the time for the stars to twinkle, for dew to settle on the grass,
For the souls of the dead to emerge from the grave, the time for their quiet song.

