Translated Content 4:
The wind beats, howling down through the ravines from the mountains;
A woman stands, gazing down at the river, on the cliff, with flowing hair;
She reminds me of a faded star, with pale and trembling lips.
She utters no sound… startled she trembles, as she gazes at the river;
How dreadfully it roars, how dreadfully it flows!
Grimacing and cruel, the black ravine rages,
“Do not kill yourself!” if only someone would advise her so.
The woman closed her eyes, and swiftly plunged into the whirlpool.

