Translated Content 0:
Indeed I see that the water brings people, shields, and swords;
In a thousand places fortresses crumble, houses stand by stone walls;
To such wretchedness, only a mourner is missing.
As if we were not in trouble, as if we were unharmed,
In the end I saw that we too were cast out with our home and hearth.
A torrent rushed from above, tore the foundation from the fortress
And mixed it too down with the shingle of the Aragvi.
It took the house with its roof, and swept us along too;
I want to cry out – help me! – but I could no longer move my tongue.
I pressed the children to my heart, begging the Icon-God for help.
Meanwhile I tried to get out, struggling toward the edge;
I cover the children's faces with the veil of a black kerchief.
And as many times as I reached the shore, so many times it was harsh;
The faces of men met me there, black as pitch.
They pushed me, threw me back into the water, and shouted this:
"Where are you coming? Go, follow the water, it is the command of God!"

Translated Content 18:
And at that moment I saw, the water before us was carrying our man away;
He turned to me and spoke, his voice was sweet and gentle –
"I beg you to forgive me, Mzia, for how I cursed you and made you angry;
Whatever you see happening to me, I deserve it, it is only right.
Do not let the children be mistreated; I beg you, look after them well for me!"
May my enemy never know the suffering I endured last night, from the dream that I saw!..

Translated Content 8:
An uneasy whispering broke out among the horsemen;
The place chosen to face the Kists bred sorrow in their hearts.
Yet what could they do? Nothing, for they had spoken and sworn an oath;
The host cannot refuse; they must march toward that spot,
Where Mindia pointed out the field of battle,
Though not a single man survive, and all be left there dead.

Translated Content 18:
An uneasy whispering broke out among the horsemen;
The place chosen to face the Kists bred dread within them.
Yet what could they do? Nothing, for they had spoken and sworn an oath;
The host cannot refuse, they must march thither,
Where Mindia pointed out the field of battle,
Even if not a single one survives, and all remain there dead.

Translated Content 7:
They said this and at that moment turned, they fled like thieves,
With swords drawn and spears held in their hands;
Hard it is, if we consider, these moments of life and death;
What can they do! To be shamed is hard, they would be dressed in gowns,
Headscarves would cover their heads, and their hats would be stripped away,
If they do not strive—like cowards, the wretched ones.
